        "\n",
        "# Multiband parameter estimation\n"
      ],
      "id": "584b7131"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from thesis_scripts import *"
      ],
      "id": "527c40a2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Literature review\n",
        "\n",
        "This was already somehow handled for PE with stellar mass binaries with LISA, e.g. [this paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2007.08544.pdf) or [this one](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2003.00357.pdf) (Mersat, Baker, Dal Canton).\n",
        "The merger time is not a good parameter to do PE, it degenerates with the chirp mass a lot.\n",
        "One can instead do PE with a time at some fixed frequency, which can be optimized.\n",
        "\n",
        "Inspiration for a way to do multibanding, perhaps?\n",
        "\n",
        "Independent group tackling the same problem: [Buscicchio+](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2106.05259.pdf) in Birmingham.\n",
        "\n",
        "## LGWA parameter estimation\n",
        "\n",
        "### Source selection\n",
        "\n",
        "We elect to start the exploration of the capabilities of the LGWA by injecting into it parameters from the two most famous detectections from the LIGO-Virgo-KAGRA collaboration:\n",
        "\n",
        "- GW150914, the first detection, a binary of black holes with component masses around $30M_{\\odot}$;\n",
        "- GW170817, the first neutron star binary detection, with component masses around $1.4M_{\\odot}$, whose electromagnetic counterpart was detected from the radio band up to the GigaelectronVolt.\n",
        "\n",
        "In order to select a single set of parameters from the posterior distributions of these sources, we compute the signal-to-noise ratio they would have if detected by the LGWA for each posterior sample.\n",
        "\n",
        "We expect the sources detected by the LVK to be typically located in sky directions favorable for it, which will not coincide with those favorable for the LGWA. On the other hand, the intrinsic distribution of the astrophysical population is expected to be roughly isotropic, as all these sources are extragalactic.\n",
        "Therefore, we randomize the sky position of the source and perform the same computation, choosing the injection parameters as those yielding the median of this distribution.\n"
      ],
      "id": "cf79ad89"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-gw170817-with-lgwa\n",
        "#| fig-cap: 'Signal-to-noise ratio for a detection of GW170817 with LGWA. The detector is assumed to run for 10 years, but most of this signal-to-noise ratio is accumulated in the last year. In both scenarios, the phase and polarization parameters are randomized. The true location of the event appeared to be favorable for LGWA, which is why randomizing it leads to SNR loss on average.'\n",
        "\n",
        "import h5py\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from tqdm import tqdm\n",
        "from thesis_scripts.lgwa_pe.lgwa_likelihood import LunarLikelihood\n",
        "from thesis_scripts.lgwa_pe.lgwa_nested_sampling import from_bilby\n",
        "import yaml\n",
        "\n",
        "like = LunarLikelihood()\n",
        "freq = np.geomspace(1e-3, 3, num=10000)\n",
        "\n",
        "# load GWTC-1 posterior for GW170817\n",
        "# from here: https://gwosc.org/eventapi/html/GWTC-1-confident/GW170817/v3/\n",
        "gw170817_file = h5py.File(data_path / 'GW170817_GWTC-1.hdf5', 'r')\n",
        "\n",
        "# keys (gw170817_file['IMRPhenomPv2NRT_lowSpin_posterior'].dtype):\n",
        "# dtype([\n",
        "# ('costheta_jn', '<f8'), 0\n",
        "# ('luminosity_distance_Mpc', '<f8'), 1\n",
        "# ('right_ascension', '<f8'), 2\n",
        "# ('declination', '<f8'), 3\n",
        "# ('m1_detector_frame_Msun', '<f8'), 4\n",
        "# ('m2_detector_frame_Msun', '<f8'), 5\n",
        "# ('lambda1', '<f8'), 6\n",
        "# ('lambda2', '<f8'), 7\n",
        "# ('spin1', '<f8'), 8\n",
        "# ('spin2', '<f8'), 9\n",
        "# ('costilt1', '<f8'), 10\n",
        "# ('costilt2', '<f8')]) 11\n",
        "\n",
        "rng = np.random.default_rng(seed=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "n_post = len(gw170817_file['IMRPhenomPv2NRT_lowSpin_posterior'])\n",
        "phase = rng.uniform(0, 2*np.pi, size=n_post)\n",
        "psi = rng.uniform(0, 2*np.pi, size=n_post)\n",
        "ra = rng.uniform(0, 2*np.pi, size=n_post)\n",
        "dec = np.pi/2. - np.arccos(rng.uniform(-1, 1, size=n_post))\n",
        "time = rng.uniform(1.5e9, 2e9, size=n_post)\n",
        "\n",
        "def params_from_sample_170817(i, sample):\n",
        "    m1, m2 = sample[4], sample[5]\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        'theta_jn': np.arccos(sample[0]),\n",
        "        'luminosity_distance': sample[1],\n",
        "        'ra': sample[2],\n",
        "        'dec': sample[3],\n",
        "        'chirp_mass': (m1*m2)**(3/5) / (m1+m2)**(1/5),\n",
        "        'mass_ratio': m2/m1,\n",
        "        'lambda_1': sample[6],\n",
        "        'lambda_2': sample[7],\n",
        "        'chi_1': sample[8]*sample[10],\n",
        "        'chi_2': sample[9]*sample[11],\n",
        "        'phase': phase[i],\n",
        "        'psi': psi[i],\n",
        "        'time_at_center': 1187008882.4,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "fname_snrs = data_path / 'cache' / 'snrs_170817.npy'\n",
        "fname_snrs_random_sky = data_path / 'cache' / 'snrs_170817_random_sky.npy'\n",
        "\n",
        "if fname_snrs.exists() and fname_snrs_random_sky.exists():\n",
        "    snrs = np.load(fname_snrs)\n",
        "    snrs_random_sky = np.load(fname_snrs_random_sky)\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    snrs = []\n",
        "    snrs_random_sky = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for i, sample in tqdm(enumerate(gw170817_file['IMRPhenomPv2NRT_lowSpin_posterior'])):\n",
        "        params = params_from_sample_170817(i, sample)\n",
        "        snrs.append(\n",
        "            like.optimal_snr(freq, from_bilby(params)))\n",
        "        snrs_random_sky.append(\n",
        "            like.optimal_snr(freq, from_bilby(\n",
        "                params | \n",
        "                {\n",
        "                    'ra': ra[i],\n",
        "                    'dec': dec[i],\n",
        "                    'time_at_center': time[i],\n",
        "                }\n",
        "            )\n",
        "        ))\n",
        "    np.save(fname_snrs, snrs)\n",
        "    np.save(fname_snrs_random_sky, snrs_random_sky)\n",
        "\n",
        "colors = ['#004D40', '#FFC107']\n",
        "\n",
        "_ = plt.hist(snrs, bins=50, alpha=.5, label='GWTC-1 posterior', density=True, color=colors[1])\n",
        "_ = plt.hist(snrs_random_sky, bins=50, alpha=.5, label='GWTC-1 posterior, randomized time and location', density=True, color=colors[0])\n",
        "\n",
        "i_median = np.argsort(snrs_random_sky)[len(snrs) //2]\n",
        "plt.axvline(snrs_random_sky[i_median], c='black', ls='--', label='Selected injection')\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "with open(data_path / 'gw170817_lgwa_median.yaml', 'w') as f:\n",
        "\n",
        "    params = params_from_sample_170817(i_median, gw170817_file['IMRPhenomPv2NRT_lowSpin_posterior'][i_median])\n",
        "    params.update({\n",
        "        'ra': ra[i_median],\n",
        "        'dec': dec[i_median],\n",
        "        'time_at_center': time[i_median],\n",
        "    })\n",
        "    yaml.dump(\n",
        "        {key: float(val) for key, val in \n",
        "            params.items()\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    f\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "_ = plt.xlabel('LGWA SNR')\n",
        "_ = plt.ylabel('Probability density')\n",
        "_ = plt.legend()\n",
        "_ = plt.xlim(0, 35)\n",
        "\n",
        "_ = plt.title('GW170817')"
      ],
      "id": "fig-gw170817-with-lgwa",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-gw150914-with-lgwa\n",
        "#| fig-cap: 'Signal-to-noise ratio for a detection of GW150914 with LGWA. The detector is assumed to run for 10 years, but most of this signal-to-noise ratio is accumulated in the last months. In both scenarios, the phase and polarization parameters are randomized. The true location of the event appeared to be unfavorable for LGWA, which is why randomizing it leads to SNR gain on average.'\n",
        "\n",
        "import h5py\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from tqdm import tqdm\n",
        "from thesis_scripts.lgwa_pe.lgwa_likelihood import LunarLikelihood\n",
        "from thesis_scripts.lgwa_pe.lgwa_nested_sampling import from_bilby\n",
        "\n",
        "like = LunarLikelihood()\n",
        "freq = np.geomspace(1e-3, 3, num=10000)\n",
        "\n",
        "# load GWTC-1 posterior for GW170817\n",
        "# from here: https://gwosc.org/eventapi/html/GWTC-1-confident/GW170817/v3/\n",
        "gw150914_file = h5py.File(data_path / 'GW150914_GWTC-1.hdf5', 'r')\n",
        "\n",
        "# keys (gw150914_file['Overall_posterior'].dtype):\n",
        "# dtype([\n",
        "# ('costheta_jn', '<f8'), 0\n",
        "# ('luminosity_distance_Mpc', '<f8'), 1\n",
        "# ('right_ascension', '<f8'), 2\n",
        "# ('declination', '<f8'), 3\n",
        "# ('m1_detector_frame_Msun', '<f8'), 4\n",
        "# ('m2_detector_frame_Msun', '<f8'), 5\n",
        "# ('spin1', '<f8'), 6\n",
        "# ('spin2', '<f8'), 7\n",
        "# ('costilt1', '<f8'), 8\n",
        "# ('costilt2', '<f8')]) 9\n",
        "\n",
        "n_post = len(gw150914_file['Overall_posterior'])\n",
        "phase = rng.uniform(0, 2*np.pi, size=n_post)\n",
        "psi = rng.uniform(0, 2*np.pi, size=n_post)\n",
        "ra = rng.uniform(0, 2*np.pi, size=n_post)\n",
        "dec = np.pi/2. - np.arccos(rng.uniform(-1, 1, size=n_post))\n",
        "time = rng.uniform(1.5e9, 2e9, size=n_post)\n",
        "\n",
        "def params_from_sample_150914(i, sample):\n",
        "    m1, m2 = sample[4], sample[5]\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        'theta_jn': np.arccos(sample[0]),\n",
        "        'luminosity_distance': sample[1],\n",
        "        'ra': sample[2],\n",
        "        'dec': sample[3],\n",
        "        'chirp_mass': (m1*m2)**(3/5) / (m1+m2)**(1/5),\n",
        "        'mass_ratio': m2/m1,\n",
        "        'lambda_1': 0.,\n",
        "        'lambda_2': 0.,\n",
        "        'chi_1': sample[6]*sample[8],\n",
        "        'chi_2': sample[7]*sample[9],\n",
        "        'phase': phase[i],\n",
        "        'psi': psi[i],\n",
        "        'time_at_center': 1126259462.4,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "fname_snrs = data_path / 'cache' / 'snrs_150914.npy'\n",
        "fname_snrs_random_sky = data_path / 'cache' / 'snrs_150914_random_sky.npy'\n",
        "\n",
        "if fname_snrs.exists() and fname_snrs_random_sky.exists():\n",
        "    snrs = np.load(fname_snrs)\n",
        "    snrs_random_sky = np.load(fname_snrs_random_sky)\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "    snrs = []\n",
        "    snrs_random_sky = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for i, sample in tqdm(enumerate(gw150914_file['Overall_posterior'])):\n",
        "        params = params_from_sample_150914(i, sample)\n",
        "        snrs.append(\n",
        "            like.optimal_snr(freq, from_bilby(params)))\n",
        "        snrs_random_sky.append(\n",
        "            like.optimal_snr(freq, from_bilby(\n",
        "                params | \n",
        "                {\n",
        "                    'ra': ra[i],\n",
        "                    'dec': dec[i],\n",
        "                    'time_at_center': time[i],\n",
        "                }\n",
        "            )\n",
        "        ))\n",
        "    np.save(fname_snrs, snrs)\n",
        "    np.save(fname_snrs_random_sky, snrs_random_sky)\n",
        "\n",
        "colors = ['#004D40', '#FFC107']\n",
        "\n",
        "_ = plt.hist(snrs, bins=50, alpha=.5, label='GWTC-1 posterior', density=True, color=colors[1])\n",
        "_ = plt.hist(snrs_random_sky, bins=50, alpha=.5, label='GWTC-1 posterior, randomized time and location', density=True, color=colors[0])\n",
        "\n",
        "i_median = np.argsort(snrs_random_sky)[len(snrs) //2]\n",
        "plt.axvline(snrs_random_sky[i_median], c='black', ls='--', label='Selected injection', ymax=0.75)\n",
        "with open(data_path / 'gw150914_lgwa_median.yaml', 'w') as f:\n",
        "\n",
        "    params = params_from_sample_150914(i_median, gw150914_file['Overall_posterior'][i_median])\n",
        "    params.update({\n",
        "        'ra': ra[i_median],\n",
        "        'dec': dec[i_median],\n",
        "        'time_at_center': time[i_median],\n",
        "    })\n",
        "    yaml.dump(\n",
        "        {key: float(val) for key, val in \n",
        "            params.items()\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    f\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "_ = plt.xlabel('LGWA SNR')\n",
        "_ = plt.ylabel('Probability density')\n",
        "_ = plt.legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "_ = plt.xlim(0, 60)\n",
        "\n",
        "_ = plt.title('GW150914')"
      ],
      "id": "fig-gw150914-with-lgwa",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
