    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### General injection results\n",
        "\n",
        "I performed a zero-noise injection with LGWA, assuming the lunar response is known.\n"
      ],
      "id": "a041c11d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from getdist import plots, MCSamples\n",
        "import yaml\n",
        "\n",
        "run_folder = data_path / 'bns_test'\n",
        "fname = run_folder / 'chains' /'weighted_post.txt'\n",
        "assert fname.exists()\n",
        "post_pandas = pd.read_csv(fname, sep=' ')\n",
        "weights = post_pandas['weight']\n",
        "\n",
        "post_equal = pd.read_csv(fname.parent / 'equal_weighted_post.txt', sep = ' ')\n",
        "\n",
        "injection_params = yaml.safe_load((run_folder / 'injection_parameters.yaml').read_text())\n",
        "\n",
        "param_names = list(post_pandas.columns)\n",
        "param_names.remove('weight')\n",
        "param_names.remove('logl')\n",
        "param_names.remove('aux_logweight')\n",
        "\n",
        "ranges = {}\n",
        "for name in param_names:\n",
        "    post = post_pandas[name]\n",
        "    avg = np.average(post, weights=weights)\n",
        "    std = np.sqrt(np.average((post-avg)**2, weights=weights))\n",
        "    lo = max(min(post), avg - 3*std)\n",
        "    hi = min(max(post), avg + 3*std)\n",
        "    ranges[name] = (lo, hi)\n",
        "\n",
        "samples_full = MCSamples(\n",
        "    samples = post_pandas[param_names].to_numpy(),\n",
        "    names = param_names,\n",
        "    labels = param_names,\n",
        "    ranges = ranges,\n",
        "    weights = weights.to_numpy(),\n",
        "    loglikes = post_pandas['logl'].to_numpy(),\n",
        "    # sampler='nested'\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "b158da36",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "g = plots.get_subplot_plotter()\n",
        "g.triangle_plot(\n",
        "    [samples_full],\n",
        "    ['ra', 'dec'],\n",
        "    smooth_scale_1d=1.,\n",
        "    smooth_scale_2d=1.,\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "a53aba90",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Geometry of lunar time measurement\n",
        "\n",
        "The \"time\" parameter we use during parameter estimation is the time of merger, computed at a point we choose to be the location of the Moon as it receives the merger signal.\n",
        "\n",
        "The scale of the uncertainty in merger time is quite small (less than a second), so assuming this to be known is not a significant approximation - even in real PE, we will be able to choose a fiducial reference frame to within a really good approximation.\n",
        "\n",
        "Our reference frame is a rigid shift of the ICRS frame to the new coordinate center; as the source is for all intents and purposes infinitely far away we can still use right ascension and declination as coordinates.\n",
        "\n",
        "Let us consider this frame as fixed.\n",
        "The other assumption we are making is that the parameter is the time of merger; however, the merger does not actually happen in band for LGWA, therefore we are driven to ask if there is a better way.\n",
        "\n",
        "We can define the time at frequency $f$ as \n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "t(f) = t_\\text{mrg} + \\underbrace{ \\frac{1}{2\\pi} \\frac{\\text{d}\\varphi(f; \\theta)}{\\text{d}f} }_{ \\text{time to merger} }\\,,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where the phase $\\varphi(f, \\theta)$ is the one from the frequency-domain waveform, computed at 3.5PN order.\n",
        "Is this parameter better measured than the time of merger for some frequencies? Yes, as the following figure shows: \n"
      ],
      "id": "c10832b5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from thesis_scripts.lgwa_pe.simple_bns_waveforms import Phif3hPN\n",
        "from numdifftools import Derivative\n",
        "\n",
        "def time_to_merger(mchirp, q, f=np.inf):\n",
        "    eta = q / (1+q)**2\n",
        "    M = mchirp / eta**(3/5)\n",
        "    func = lambda freq : Phif3hPN(\n",
        "            freq,\n",
        "            M,\n",
        "            eta,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    return Derivative(func)(f) / (2*np.pi)\n",
        "\n",
        "freqs = np.geomspace(0.5, 4, num=100)\n",
        "samples_to_use = 1000\n",
        "m = post_equal['chirp_mass'].to_numpy()[:samples_to_use]\n",
        "q = post_equal['mass_ratio'].to_numpy()[:samples_to_use]\n",
        "t = post_equal['time_at_center'].to_numpy()[:samples_to_use]\n",
        "\n",
        "correlations = [\n",
        "    np.corrcoef(\n",
        "        m, \n",
        "        t + time_to_merger(m, q, freq)\n",
        "        )[0, 1] for freq in freqs]\n",
        "\n",
        "correlations_q = [\n",
        "    np.corrcoef(\n",
        "        q, \n",
        "        t + time_to_merger(m, q, freq)\n",
        "        )[0, 1] for freq in freqs]\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "correlations_ttm = [\n",
        "    np.corrcoef(\n",
        "        m, \n",
        "        time_to_merger(m, q, freq)\n",
        "        )[0, 1] for freq in freqs]\n",
        "\n",
        "correlations_ttm_q = [\n",
        "    np.corrcoef(\n",
        "        q, \n",
        "        time_to_merger(m, q, freq)\n",
        "        )[0, 1] for freq in freqs]\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "stds = [\n",
        "    np.std(t + time_to_merger(m, q, freq)) \n",
        "    for freq in freqs]\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, axs = plt.subplots(2, 1, sharex=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "c_1 = '#117733'\n",
        "c_2 = '#DDCC77'\n",
